{
  "id": "20997_henkasuru",
  "headword": "{変化|へんか}する",
  "reading": "へんかする",
  "romaji": "henkasuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to change; to transform; to vary",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to change; to undergo change; to transform; to vary",
      "explanation": "For something to become different from its previous state. Used for gradual or noticeable changes in condition, form, quality, or nature."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "20997_henkasuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{季節|きせつ}とともに{景色|けしき}が{変化|へんか}する。",
      "english": "The scenery changes with the seasons.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20997_henkasuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{社会|しゃかい}は{常|つね}に{変化|へんか}している。",
      "english": "Society is constantly changing.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20997_henkasuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "テクノロジーの{発展|はってん}により、{私|わたし}たちの{生活|せいかつ}は{大|おお}きく{変化|へんか}した。",
      "english": "Due to technological development, our lives have changed greatly.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A する verb composed of {変|へん} (change) + {化|か} (transform, -ification). One of the most common する verbs. Primarily intransitive — the thing itself changes. To change something actively, use {変|か}える.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {大|おお}きく{変化|へんか}する: to change greatly\n- {急激|きゅうげき}に{変化|へんか}する: to change rapidly\n- {変化|へんか}に{富|と}む: to be full of variety/change\n- {変化|へんか}に{対応|たいおう}する: to respond to change\n- {変化|へんか}が{激|はげ}しい: to have dramatic changes\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {変|か}わる: to change — everyday native Japanese word; more casual\n- {変動|へんどう}する: to fluctuate — implies repeated or unstable changes (prices, temperatures)\n- {転換|てんかん}する: to convert, to shift — a deliberate, decisive change in direction\n- {進化|しんか}する: to evolve — change that implies improvement or advancement",
  "conjugation_type": "suru",
